<article class="detail-page"><a class="detail-back" href="/insights/">← Back to insights</a><div class="section-label">Supply Chain</div><h1>Inventory Carrying Costs Are Destroying Your Margins. Here's How to Calculate and Fix Them</h1><div class="detail-content modal-body"><p>Most MSME owners think excess inventory is a minor inconvenience. The numbers tell a different story.</p><h4>What Does Inventory Actually Cost?</h4><p>The true carrying cost of inventory is typically 20–35% of inventory value per year — once you account for: capital cost (opportunity cost of cash tied up), storage cost, insurance, obsolescence risk, and handling cost. For a business carrying ₹5Cr of inventory, this is ₹1–1.75Cr per year in hidden cost.</p><h4>The Three Levers</h4><p>Lever 1 — Demand forecasting: An 8-week rolling forecast aligned to sales data reduces safety stock requirements by 30–40% without increasing stockout risk. Lever 2 — ABC classification: Focus tight inventory management on A-class items (top 20% of SKUs driving 80% of revenue). Looser control on C-class items is acceptable. Lever 3 — Supplier lead time reduction: Every week of lead time reduction allows a corresponding reduction in safety stock. Reducing lead time from 18 to 9 days (as we achieved for one client) halves the safety stock requirement.</p></div><a class="btn-primary" href="/#contact">Request a Discovery Call →</a></article>
